{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/185935-newbie-questions","id":185935,"title":"Newbie Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-01T19:10:36-07:00","id":185935,"title":"Newbie Questions","content":"Evening, Scion fans. I'm swinging through from the Exalted board with a question or two about the gameline.<br /> <br /> I picked up Hero on a whim because I'd heard interesting things about the game but I'm not sure whether to go for the rest of the resources. Fate is kind of a bitch of a mechanic for example, it doesn't really seem to encourage the usual kind of &quot;let's ride a dinosaur down main street!&quot; action that you get from playing a Solar, which is one of the big things I really love about Exalted.<br /> <br /> The main thing I'm wondering is how viable it is for Scions to eventually get out from under mom's/dad's shadow and become their own gods. I know there's mechanical support for ascension in the other PDFs, but judging from Hero every Scion at least starts out defined by their parent's favored abilities and there's pressure to share all the same virtues. There's probably not a lot of Sun Wukong figures coming out of Japan for instance (never mind him being Chinese). Is that more or less how it plays out in the rest of the source books? Is Loki only ever going to produce baby trickster gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T21:00:47-07:00","id":185978,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm glad to see someone trying out Scion for the first time. Glad to help with any questions you may have about RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/185935-newbie-questions#post185935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate is kind of a bitch of a mechanic for example, it doesn't really seem to encourage the usual kind of &quot;let's ride a dinosaur down main street!&quot; action that you get from playing a Solar, which is one of the big things I really love about Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate is very tricky for a number of reasons. Firstly, RAW Scion, Fate has very little... effect in all honesty. You get some dice penalties, but they don't do all that much in the system. The Fatebinding system falls into that situation of, &quot;Cool idea, bad mechanics.&quot; which all of RAW Scion exemplifies. While the idea of Fate is exceptionally important to many Pantheons, and the very functioning of the Scion world itself, if you want to stick with RAW stuff, you can almost just ignore Fatebindings. They won't really do much, unfortunately. It tries to encourage some kinds of behavior, some of which, as you said, make no sense to discourage. But, ultimately, at the end of the road at God, you can pretty much just ignore your Fatebindings and just suffer some dice penalties. Something so minor it doesn't make sense that the Gods withdrew from the world over. (Unless you are the Tuatha, Bogovi, Anunna, or the few other Pantheons that have legitimate, real world mythology reasons for not being involved any more)<br /> <br /> But, if you would like to use Fatebindings in your games of Scion, many people have presented houseruled versions of Fatebindings for people to use. Everyone has a different take on how they should work, so I will let others present theirs if they are around. But, the one that has been created for Scion 2.0 is presented <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home/fate\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Our version of Fate is designed to encourage repetitive behavior, and discourage people breaking from the path they have forged for themselves. So, for example, Zeus likely has developed a very powerful Fate for committing serial adultery, meaning that whenever he has the opportunity, he is likely going to succumb to this Fate of his. But, since we didn't want Fates to be all bad, in that situation Zeus could also use his Fate in serial adultery in order to improve his attempts at covering it up from Hera, seducing people, kidnapping people, anything that reasonably involves committing serial adultery.<br /> <br /> I believe Telgar also has a version of Fatebindings, and Gotham By Night did as well, but they recently took their site down unfortunately.<br /> <br /> But, yes. Fate in RAW is both toothless, and discourages behavior that it shouldn't. In the way that I have seen Fate run is that Fate, as this not truely existing being, wants a story. It wants deep characters, and it wants drama. It wants heroes, villains, and nothing but the extravagant. Fate, the very force of the story, shouldn't discourage you from being awesome. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/185935-newbie-questions#post185935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing I'm wondering is how viable it is for Scions to eventually get out from under mom's/dad's shadow and become their own gods. I know there's mechanical support for ascension in the other PDFs, but judging from Hero every Scion at least starts out defined by their parent's favored abilities and there's pressure to share all the same virtues. There's probably not a lot of Sun Wukong figures coming out of Japan for instance (never mind him being Chinese). Is that more or less how it plays out in the rest of the source books? Is Loki only ever going to produce baby trickster gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two points I'd like to hit here. Firstly, yeah, RAW Scion really, really encourages people through sheer mechanical benefit to pick Divine Parents who have similar powers as they wish to have. While there is some mythological example for this, such as Thor having an incredibly strong daughter, Metis having a brilliantly smart and cunning daughter, and so on, it is a very unfortunate reality of RAW Scion that the players who play carbon copies, or near carbon copies of their Divine Parents are going to be at a mechanical advantage over their fellows who are not following in their parent's footsteps.<br /> <br /> As with Fatebindings, and everything in Scion, every member of the community has some houserules. Some people keep these rules, others allow people to pick their Associated Abilities and Powers, some just scrap the concept entirely. In Scion 2.0, we used <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home/character-creation\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> rules for Associated Powers (listed under &quot;Associated Attributes &amp; Purviews&quot;) which, while it does encourage people to have some similarity with their Divine Parent, does not encourage total overlap, and doesn't punish an entire void of overlap too harshly. (Which, as someone who does like playing as the Scion of a Lesser Deity just to shake things up, does help a lot.)<br /> <br /> But, second point about Virtues. Once again, everyone has their own houserules about Virtues. The most common I have seen, and the one we use is, &quot;You must have two of your Pantheon's four Virtues&quot; minimum. In doing so, this allows people to stray from the norms, while not going so far, at least at character creation, to be alien to their Divine Family. In our rules, not all Gods have all four Pantheon Virtues. Some Gods even have Dark Virtues. Odin and Tezcatlipoca for sure on that front.<br /> <br /> I do hope that helps you HK-87. If you have any more questions, be sure to ask away!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T23:47:15-07:00","id":186073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/185935-newbie-questions#post185935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evening, Scion fans. I'm swinging through from the Exalted board with a question or two about the gameline.<br /> <br /> I picked up Hero on a whim because I'd heard interesting things about the game but I'm not sure whether to go for the rest of the resources. Fate is kind of a bitch of a mechanic for example, it doesn't really seem to encourage the usual kind of &quot;let's ride a dinosaur down main street!&quot; action that you get from playing a Solar, which is one of the big things I really love about Exalted.<br /> <br /> The main thing I'm wondering is how viable it is for Scions to eventually get out from under mom's/dad's shadow and become their own gods. I know there's mechanical support for ascension in the other PDFs, but judging from Hero every Scion at least starts out defined by their parent's favored abilities and there's pressure to share all the same virtues. There's probably not a lot of Sun Wukong figures coming out of Japan for instance (never mind him being Chinese). Is that more or less how it plays out in the rest of the source books? Is Loki only ever going to produce baby trickster gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Should note that second edition is going to be different on the 'becoming their own gods' thing. The Legend rules apparently work such that you can see the relationship from Zeus to Ares to Eros, but they're by no means clones. Your Origin is an influence on your powers, but not the only one.<br /> <br /> Really, I'd hold off on getting any more 1e stuff, and wait to see how 2e turns out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T23:48:08-07:00","id":186898,"title":"","content":"Scion is a fun over the top crazy adventure setting, a lot like Exalted.<br /> <br /> Yes, Fate binding is a bitch of a mechanic to impliment, that requires a LOT of book keeping on the STs part. As an ST, I pretty much ignored the mechanics and just went with what was dramatically appropriate.. the PCs picked up groupies and fans and wards.. things that made the stories better.. and added to the characters..<br /> <br /> And yes.. the game mechanically tries to make you like your divine parent.. but nothing stops you from branching out, other the xp costs..<br /> <br /> And again.. yes,, there is a new edition coming out.. but we'll be lucky to see it before next year.. so if you can find the books or PDFs cheap.. I'd suggest getting them.. it's one of my favorite settings..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}